  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard to check how the panels render, and I haven't confirmed the rule fires on real 5xx data.\n\n**What the data holds:** The web-logs data view has one document per HTTP request. The useful fields are `timestamp`, `response` (a string, with a `response.keyword` version), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `url`, and `host`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-a9d8dce0 Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests, as a single number.\n- Requests over time.\n- Responses by status code, as a pie chart.\n- Average bytes by file extension.\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-a9d8dce0-web-logs-overview-4c3e604cafba.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-a9d8dce0 5xx spike\" checks every minute. It counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` whose `response.keyword` matches `5[0-9][0-9]` over a 5-minute window, and fires when that count is above 10. I created it disabled and then enabled it. It has no action attached, so it will show up in Kibana's alerts but won't notify anyone.",
